Z||000000||Fiero*101||09-05-2001||11:53 PM||||Ok I know I have had alot of posts this past week but im just trying to find out how to fix my car and diagnose my problems. And now I think I eather have Sensor problems or Gauge problems<BR>1.My Voltage gauge reads low but then it will read normal then low then normal and my alt belt is fine and its tight and it does not squeal.So any ideas on that?<BR>2.My gas gauge Im hoping to god is wrong i will fill it and when im driving I can watch it fall just by driving it only 10 miles will put it at a HALF A TANK!!!!any ideas on that?<BR>3.This is not a Gauge ? but does any body else or has any body else ever had a stretched throttle cable i mean when i put my foot down it takes a wile for it to get up to speed(The guy that sold it to me said it has a stretched throttle cable)any ideas on how to fix it?<P>Like alwas ANY INFO for me is GOOD INFO<BR>thanks guys you have been great help<P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||09-06-2001||12:14 AM||||I don't know about the cable but the gas gauges on the fieros are just for decoration.  Don't trust them!! Use your odometer instead.  As for your voltage gauge you might want to check your system with a reliable voltmeter.  It could be that your alt is going.  Good luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||G-Nasty||09-06-2001||12:26 AM||||the throttle cable is about 65-70 bucks new-<BR>it is very difficult to install at the pedal. Remove at one end and follow. You will need a coat hanger and a flashlight to connect to pedal mechanism. This install is a nightmare as most repairs on these plastic pontiacs usually are. Good Luck-||||reg||1
Z||000003||NEPTUNE||09-06-2001||02:42 PM||||I HAVE HAD THE SAME BATT. GAUGE PROBLEM SINCE '97- I HAVE TRIED EVERYTHING EXCEPT REWIRING AND REPLACING THE GAUGE. 57,000 MILES AND 2 ALTS LATER,IT STILL DOES THAT. I JUST FIGURED THAT IT IS FOR DECORATION, LIKE THE GAS GAUGE. I DONT THINK YOUR OTHER PROBLEM IS A STRETCHED CABLE, BUT I DON'T KNOW WHAT IT REALLY IS.  REPLACING A CABLE IS KINDA TOUGH.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||09-06-2001||03:17 PM||||Check the plastic cable housing in the engine compartment. It can melt and effectively shorten the cable travel. the cable it's self will not stretch, it will break first!<BR>Coy||||reg||1
